A1. This is really true. ~ FACT
A4. This fellow had the weight of the world on his shoulders. ~ ATLAS
A7. Your first cousin's maternal ancestor. ~ AUNT
A10. Any egg will get this way if kept in hot water. ~ HARD
A12. This holds a lot of liquor. ~ TANK
A14. Sobriquet for the college boy's Lizzie. ~ CHARIOT
A17. An entertaining woman. ~ HOSTESS
A19. Pronoun. ~ HER
A20. Supplications. ~ PRAYERS
A22. This man's wife turned to rubber. ~ LOT
A23. This is often getting boiled. ~ EGG
A25. A variety of corundum—this is very hard. ~ EMERY
A26. This never seems to dry up. ~ SEA
A27. You'll be this if you're watchful. ~ ALERT
A29. This should be well stuffed. ~ PAD
A30. Aids. ~ HELPS
A32. The lady of the moon. ~ DIANA
A34. A good thing to carry on a joy ride if you don't want to walk home. ~ SPARE
A36. Preposition. ~ TO
A37. There's a lot of money made with this. ~ DIE
A38. This leaves in the spring. ~ ELM
A39. The autocrat of the breakfast table. ~ MA
A40. A very idle fellow. ~ IDLER
A42. A seat. ~ STOOL
A44. These are in jail—and never will get out. ~ CELLS
