A68. Where Horizontal 67 would send you. ~ BYBY

D1. Famous Generalissimo. ~ FOCH
D2. Attacked fiercely. ~ CHARGED
D3. This is often at sea. ~ TAR
D4. It's easy to do this in the spring. ~ ADORE
D5. The poor crossword Indian. ~ LO
D6. This is usually told by the late returning husband in the wee small hours. ~ STORY
D7. This little fellow is noted for his industry. ~ ANT
D8. This raises a racket when it's picked on. ~ UKELELE
D9. Collegian speeders have a hard time passing this. ~ TEST
